# Head/tail Commands
=>head -n <number of lines> <path>
Ex: head/tail -n 10 /exc/os-release

# grep 
=>grep "<word>" <path>
grep "error" /etc/passwd

=> grep -n "<word>" <path> # this will give the line number of the error
=> grep -B 2 -A 2 "error" /var/log/syslog (2 before and 2 after the error)


